migrationAlgorithm:
v3 -> v4 migration runs once at boot when KEY_V4 is absent, inside load(). Idempotent and crash-safe via a read-back-confirmed safety-net delete.

ALGORITHM (load()):
  raw4 = U.safeLoad('godzilla-save-v4')
  container = raw4 ? sanitizeContainer(raw4) : null
  migratedOrFresh = false
  if (!container):
      v3 = U.safeLoad('godzilla-save-v3')
      if (v3 && v3.v === 3): container = migrateV3toV4(v3)   // WRAP raw; sanitizeGame runs on apply
      else:                  container = freshContainer()
      migratedOrFresh = true
  container = sanitizeContainer(container) || freshContainer()   // re-sanitize migrated/fresh
  _container = container; _activeIdx = indexOfActive()
  if (migratedOrFresh):
      if (writeContainerVerified(container)):                  // safeSave + READ-BACK compare
          // keep v3 this boot as a safety net; it carries migratedFrom:'v3'
      // else: keep v3, retry next boot (v4 absent => re-migrate from still-present v3)
  applySlotToState(_container.slots[_activeIdx].game)
  // CONFIRMED-write reap: only on a SUBSEQUENT boot where raw4.v===4 && raw4.migratedFrom==='v3'
  if (raw4 && raw4.v===4 && raw4.migratedFrom==='v3'):
      try { localStorage.removeItem('godzilla-save-v3') } catch(e){}
      delete _container.migratedFrom
  save(); requestPersist(); asyncIdbRecover(); return true

migrateV3toV4(v3):
  game = {}; for k in v3: if (k!=='v') game[k]=v3[k]   // copy verbatim, drop the v field
  now = Date.now()
  return { v:4, rev:1, activeSlot:slotId, migratedFrom:'v3',
           slots:[ { id:slotId, name:'Save 1', createdAt:now,
                     lastPlayed:(typeof v3.lastSeen==='number'&&isFinite(v3.lastSeen))?v3.lastSeen:now,
                     lastBackupAt:0, backupPromptSeen:false, prestige:0, game:game } ] }
  // game is RAW; the SAME sanitizeGame that every load uses clamps it on apply.
  // This preserves (does NOT re-trigger) the gz2014 force-unshift and the formAxisSeen one-time
  // rebalance toast (economy.js:490-496) for a pre-formula migrated player — they fire identically
  // to today because applySlotToState runs the unchanged sanitizer.

writeContainerVerified(c):
  if (!U.safeSave(KEY_V4, c)) return false            // quota/private -> keep v3, retry next boot
  back = U.safeLoad(KEY_V4)                            // READ IT STRAIGHT BACK — 'confirmed' means read-back,
  return !!(back && back.v===4 && Array.isArray(back.slots) && back.slots.length===c.slots.length)
  // safeSave's boolean alone is insufficient: it only catches the setItem throw, not a silent
  // partial write or accept-then-evict. The read-back makes migration crash-safe & lossless.

freshContainer(): one default slot ('Save 1', defaults from economy.js:53-69 minus runtime-only fields), v:4, rev:0.

sanitizeContainer(raw): return null on structural failure (!obj || v!==4 || slots not array || empty) -> caller falls to migrate/fresh. Otherwise: slots.slice(0,SLOTS_MAX).map(sanitizeSlot); re-stamp any 0/blank/duplicate id to a fresh unique id (a VALID unique id is preserved as-is); coerce activeSlot to a real slot id (out-of-range -> slots[0].id). A single bad slot is REPAIRED in place by sanitizeSlot (bad game->fresh via sanitizeGame, bad name->'Save N'), never dropped — only a wholly-unparseable container falls back.

If BOTH v3 and v4 exist (re-run after a crash that wrote v4 but didn't reap v3): v4 ALWAYS wins; v3 ignored (no double-migration loop overwriting v4 with stale v3).
